{
  "slug": "artist:dj-godfather",
  "name": "DJ Godfather",
  "editorial_article": "Based in Detroit, Michigan, DJ Godfather is a producer and DJ credited with popularizing the high-energy electronic subgenre known as Ghettotech. He has maintained a long-term presence in the Detroit dance scene, with his influence extending to early collaborations with the late Ann Arbor-based producer Disco D. Throughout his career, he has utilized his own label, Databass Records, to release various projects that highlight the rhythmic and percussive nature of the Detroit electronic sound. Beyond his own solo work, his reputation as an influential figure is grounded in his commitment to the local music scene that developed from the legacy of pioneering Detroit DJs like Ken Collier. His contributions remain foundational to the evolution of the city's dance music output.",
